15. EFFECT RESET BLOCK IS NOT THE FIRST SUSPECT
==================================================

There is a per-frame reset block that restores:

    rotation from obj.rx / obj.ry
    scale from obj.scale

when no effect owns those components.

That is actually compatible with toolbar edits PROVIDED the scene state changed,
because the reset uses the stored values.

So do not alter the effect guards merely to make toolbar rotation/scale persist.

If updateObj writes:

    obj.rx = 5

then the reset should restore to 5 degrees, not zero.

Likewise:

    obj.scale = 1.1

should reset to 1.1.

Only revisit this if measured state and rendered group disagree.

